{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And for his sister, a virgin, who is near to him.</b> Because she is his sister from the same father and mother. <b>Who is near to him:</b> what Rashi explained — to include the arusah (betrothed) — does not refer to the arus (betrothed husband), for we have an established ruling: his wife who is arusah — he does not mourn and does not defile himself for her. And likewise we learned in Torat Kohanim: 'כי אם לשארו' — excluding his arusah. Rather, it refers to him, the priest's sister. And likewise the interpretation of <b>and for his sister, a virgin</b> — this is a minor, unmarried, who is near to him, to include the arusah. For if it had not written 'who is near to him,' I might have said: since she became betrothed, he does not defile himself for her. It comes to teach 'who is near to him' — she is still near to him and not to her husband, since he has not married her; for had she been married, she would be near to her husband and he would defile himself for her, as it is written, כי אם לשארו." "<b>Who has not been to a man.</b> Who was not had by a man; but if she had been to a man, he does not defile himself for her, for he is already close to her and would defile himself for her." "<b>For her he shall defile himself.</b> It is a commandment, for if he did not wish to defile himself, they defile him against his will. And there was an incident involving Yosef the priest, whose wife died on the eve of Passover and he did not wish to defile himself for her, and the Sages pushed him and defiled him against his will entirely." "<b>For her he shall defile himself.</b> And he does not defile himself for others along with her — lest he say: since I have become defiled, I will gather the bone of so-and-so with my own hands. Therefore it says: for her he shall defile himself. <b>For her he shall defile himself.</b> And he does not defile himself for her limbs, and likewise not for his father and mother while they are alive; but he does defile himself even for a bone the size of a barley grain from a corpse."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:00.733803979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}